{"kind":"stack","id":"gravity-stack","title":"Gravity: why things fall","theme":{"background":"#F4F9FF","foreground":"#1A2B3C","font":"Verdana, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Gravity is a pulling force between the Earth and every object. It pulls things down towards the ground."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"What is the force that pulls a dropped ball down to the ground?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Gravity","why":"Gravity is the force pulling objects towards the Earth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Magnetism","why":"Pupils mix up magnets with gravity, but magnets only pull some metals.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Friction","why":"Friction slows things down when they rub, not what pulls them down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"When you let go of a pencil in the air, which way does it move?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Down towards the ground","why":"Gravity pulls every unsupported object towards the Earth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Up into the air","why":"Pupils may think things float up if they are light, but gravity still pulls them down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Sideways across the room","why":"Pupils may think a falling object moves sideways, but its main pull is down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"apple"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"An apple hangs on a branch. Wind shakes it loose. What should it do next?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Fall to the ground","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Float up into the sky","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Yes! Gravity pulls the apple down, so it falls to the ground."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Not quite. Gravity does not lift the apple. The apple still falls down to the ground."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Unsupported"},{"type":"text","id":"c7-e","content":"An unsupported object has nothing holding it up, so gravity pulls it down to the Earth."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which object is unsupported and will fall?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"A book released from your hand","why":"Nothing holds the book up once you let go, so gravity pulls it down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"A book resting on a table","why":"A table supports the book, so it does not fall.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"A book held up by a shelf","why":"The shelf supports the book, so it stays still.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Is the force of gravity between the Earth and a ball bigger or smaller than the ball's own pull?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Bigger","why":"The Earth is huge, so its pull on the ball is far greater than the ball's pull on the Earth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Smaller","why":"Pupils may think small things pull less, but the Earth's mass makes its pull stronger.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What is the name of the force pulling a falling stone towards the Earth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Gravity","why":"Gravity is the pulling force between the Earth and objects.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Air resistance","why":"Air resistance slows a falling object but does not pull it down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Weight of the air","why":"Pupils may confuse air with the pull, but air does not cause falling.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"A ball is dropped from a window. Which force makes it fall?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Gravity","why":"Gravity acts between the Earth and the ball, so the ball falls.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Magnetism","why":"Pupils may think magnets pull the ball, but the ball is not magnetic.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Wind","why":"Wind can move objects, but the ball falls even on still days.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Well done! You finished the gravity lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"Keep looking for things that fall around you. Each one shows gravity at work."}],"actions":[]}}
